{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:27:50.217002Z","id":"6d821d11ac0aa475d543a8024ad1579d0a1a1d28619975fd6a0b137d8c624c6e","body":{"detail":"crates/toolpath-git/tests/vcs_mapping.rs, vcs@mapping row 1. 'Structured intent, refs, multi-perspective': the step carries meta.intent and a raw diff per file; refs and a structural perspective are not produced by the git import.","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":928},"end":{"line":928},"content_hash":"dbbe961e3fe9f4fe25342b8831082babc2e6a4122d090ccea17680d63781006a"},"summary":"Commit → Step holds: one step per commit, parents mirror git's (merge step has both parents)","tags":["rfc-vcs","goldens","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:27:50.228250Z","id":"681054840a323fa7eb681eab6295ea303d84188c77aff15decbec71959652c89","body":{"detail":"vcs@mapping row 2. The 'dead end preservation' half does not hold for git import: a deleted branch's commits are gone (row 6), and the import walks branch tips only, so it never produces dead ends.","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":929},"end":{"line":929},"content_hash":"c8a3db4629eb50c16643abb9ccdd0c07df6d67b5a75f574a47e2238be64c4bf6"},"summary":"Branch → Path holds for base context: one path per branch, base = repo + branch point ref + branch name","tags":["rfc-vcs","goldens","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:27:50.240304Z","id":"d5d61d2a3dec061ca643d112b6a97e7692bd35cac6b2c3df00d8698c084c94b7","body":{"detail":"toolpath-git commit_to_step takes message.lines().next(). A commit 'Main moves on' + two body lines imports as intent 'Main moves on'. Either keep the full message (or put the body in meta.description) or scope the RFC row to the subject. vcs@mapping row 3.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":930},"end":{"line":930},"content_hash":"9e8af95a6761ec622e6519639fcd34d88303707df22f3637ed75e954763ce4d2"},"suggested_fix":"intent = subject; description = body (meta.description exists per the RFC Meta Object table)","summary":"Commit message → meta.intent keeps only the subject line; the body is dropped","tags":["rfc-vcs","goldens","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:27:50.251606Z","id":"5f1ea358c5f2e9229930eccfcb3ca23ddbd42f59f24711ece2daf578873a3c70","body":{"detail":"A commit signed with a throwaway SSH key (vcs@mapping row 4) imports with no meta.signatures. Not implemented on purpose: a git signature covers the commit object, while an RFC step signature covers JCS({step, change}); copying the armored sig into meta.signatures as scope author would make RFC verification fail. Options: carry it as a VCS attestation (e.g. meta.source.extra.gpgsig) or define a 'vcs-commit' signature scope in the RFC.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":931},"end":{"line":931},"content_hash":"dfbc322d5c7653e059617d34fd76fbe92b62d4bcc183ae819b236a3a4651b6fd"},"summary":"GPG/SSH signature → meta.signatures does not hold: the git import never reads gpgsig","tags":["rfc-vcs","goldens","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:27:50.262287Z","id":"705d52b707f4ecbcb80cd2d9be40f4d2ef3be6d49326b576a363ac52480485e8","body":{"detail":"vcs@mapping row 5: human:alex and human:bob with name and an email identity. 'Multiple systems' is one system (email) from git; committer identity is not imported.","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":932},"end":{"line":932},"content_hash":"0cad0873e646fdff8cd77086d884488a0d5b3a902cc5f029f4eb836b25085c0a"},"summary":"Author identity → meta.actors holds: each author is an actor string with a definition (name, email identity)","tags":["rfc-vcs","goldens","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:27:50.271135Z","id":"7402a2031f82bf8be55b090424065bacb86ca3958bde3f9acc11f99c2bcd4fb6","body":{"detail":"vcs@mapping row 6: a branch deleted before import leaves no trace (git already lost it unless the reflog is read), and unmerged commits on deleted refs are not walked. The RFC's 'Toolpath preserves dead ends' holds for documents Toolpath records live, not for ones derived from git after the fact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":937},"end":{"line":937},"content_hash":"b22bb5ee685f66fe9bdce4121077e340f69917a6ecd4635f5e9587f070a38ba6"},"summary":"Dead ends from VCS history are not preserved by the git import","tags":["rfc-vcs","goldens","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:28:03.242849Z","id":"4188fae59914bcfc4bd303eb0604024b9c84af31c0b77762fa0edc94b6d85451","body":{"detail":"core_types@validate (crates/path-cli/tests/core_types.rs): a duplicated step id, a duplicated path id, a parent naming no step, and a head naming no step all validate. The JSON Schema cannot express these; the validator would need a structural pass after the schema.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":127},"end":{"line":127},"content_hash":"348caab9de8420e7f36d5a15f2b61a3eb6b1f56a1b3eaaf37d48e52104d2ce62"},"summary":"path p validate does not enforce ID uniqueness, parent references or path.head","tags":["rfc-types","goldens","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:28:03.253618Z","id":"fe818f2b8049614e6361840c310502a6f1bfcbdbb17e9674d8ef4a7fdaf453f6","body":{"detail":"core_types@validate row '$ref MUST NOT point to a .path.jsonl stream': accepted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":122},"end":{"line":122},"content_hash":"ebd9ce2deed09df50a67c84bcb86c6b8394d21294f3f99f4c96da9a3c91c4167"},"summary":"path p validate accepts a $ref to a .path.jsonl stream, which the RFC forbids","tags":["rfc-types","goldens","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:28:03.272645Z","id":"7b0b2a9eb1f9a0c89520027e59012af281ab3833397cb4ca3669160f07158948","body":{"detail":"formats@examples: the committed examples' .path.json twins use graph id graph-<path id>; Graph::from_jsonl names it <path id>. Everything else round-trips; all nine golden documents seal back identical (formats@<set>). examples/path-02-local-session.path.jsonl had also drifted (missing base.ref) and is fixed in this piece.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":116},"end":{"line":116},"content_hash":"da2a3bc8739fc4b4cbedee6bdc50564e311ab1bcf3c2059dd855f5991a45bf81"},"summary":"A .path.jsonl stream carries no graph identity; sealing names the graph after its path","tags":["rfc-types","goldens","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.422642Z","id":"984baee1559b72ffa375cd5555e1f9e4e81a24a62ebfc10ffd353f26ec5de76f","body":{"detail":"crates/toolpath/tests/jcs.rs::rfc8785_reference_vectors (vectors from cyberphone/json-canonicalization 32a4819, Apache-2.0, vendored in tests/jcs-vectors). Behind the toolpath 'verify' feature.","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":712},"end":{"line":713},"content_hash":"a733e9c2739cd417c541a2bfc407ff5214a2f4ebd2695403f2193bd2313f43bc"},"summary":"JCS (RFC 8785) is the canonicalizer: toolpath::v1::sign::jcs reproduces all six RFC 8785 reference vectors byte for byte","tags":["rfc","signatures","jcs","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.422738Z","id":"a25ba26430c759fbb5a70689bdad82f6db78d3d91589c21fc3b44cda0cf0ddec","body":{"detail":"The implementation follows RFC 8785 (UTF-16), as the RFC 8785 vector weird.json requires (U+1F602 sorts before U+FB33). An implementer following this line literally would produce different canonical bytes and their signatures would not verify against ours. Proven by crates/toolpath/tests/jcs.rs::key_order_is_utf16_not_utf8.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":719},"end":{"line":719},"content_hash":"86ccd1ad0524436a93b319614f8bf7400164f587a4fca7389c64583e19fdecd9"},"suggested_fix":"**Key Ordering**: Object keys sorted by their UTF-16 code units (RFC 8785 §3.2.3)","summary":"False as written: RFC 8785 sorts object keys by UTF-16 code units, not UTF-8 bytes; the two orders differ for keys above U+FFFF versus U+E000–U+FFFF","tags":["rfc","signatures","jcs","spec-error","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.423500Z","id":"9a4907f563c0b8ec6834339e8e8c49309f8feb21ff19d4685571d59ad1872fe4","body":{"detail":"crates/toolpath/tests/jcs.rs::properties_over_generated_values (no whitespace outside strings; re-parse equal; idempotent; structure equals an independent writer).","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":720},"end":{"line":720},"content_hash":"e23f9ae02d6d9bb29056a1a2e92b17de537a80dfc93ea2338cebaa63b55a05a7"},"summary":"No whitespace between tokens: checked on 2000 generated values","tags":["rfc","signatures","jcs","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.423690Z","id":"29e1e4a2defdccdbd15e6a9007a793e43341d2e420c181989c37bcc0900969f4","body":{"detail":"crates/toolpath/tests/jcs.rs::escape_set_is_minimal over U+0000–U+007F. Note the rule omits that RFC 8785 writes five controls in short form (\\b \\t \\n \\f \\r), as this RFC's own example does with \\n; only the other controls use \\u00xx.","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":721},"end":{"line":722},"content_hash":"d6f89f5d41f36940c394a6a99d4d300b85707aef7f270d52b0fd3f8563638997"},"summary":"Escape set is minimal: only quote, backslash and U+0000–U+001F, lowercase hex","tags":["rfc","signatures","jcs","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.423757Z","id":"3ca5d740084391d9475bbdbbd67e3d3bb2434cb3dd71910aa8f0f4bd099a9884","body":{"detail":"crates/toolpath/tests/jcs.rs::numbers_serialize_as_es6 (-0→0, 4.50→4.5, 2e-3→0.002, 1e-7, 1e21→1e+21, 333333333.33333329→333333333.3333333) and the values/weird vectors. The rule text is a paraphrase; the normative definition is ES6 (exponent form at or above 1e21 and below 1e-6).","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":723},"end":{"line":724},"content_hash":"741729400fd680a989d3489dfd0b13ddd4c39463180f9899340588076327fe44"},"summary":"Numbers serialize as ECMAScript Number.toString (RFC 8785 §3.2.2.3)","tags":["rfc","signatures","jcs","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.423803Z","id":"32727f9c21d727b2027c450a9a908545c2600d3401bc55df29a0402bf5ee7559","body":{"detail":"crates/toolpath/tests/jcs.rs::escape_set_is_minimal and the unicode/french/weird vectors.","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":725},"end":{"line":725},"content_hash":"3a224c580e1223389c799e7d040f86cccfe71afce5ce3b38e78669399606afda"},"summary":"Strings are UTF-8, minimally escaped: non-ASCII stays literal","tags":["rfc","signatures","jcs","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.423853Z","id":"a4c9afc1e34b618600dd1bb09f732ad350ac32a563e64a621a4a8a7f352a2e41","body":{"detail":"toolpath::v1::sign::step_author_input + digest; crates/toolpath/tests/jcs.rs::what_gets_signed, tests/signatures.rs::signed_step_and_path_verify, ::step_meta_is_not_signed, ::tampered_change_fails.","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":729},"end":{"line":743},"content_hash":"1fd6c5120784def06929f54ffb8822fec10daecfaea1657939c7ee79a26f9d43"},"summary":"Step author input is JCS({change, step}) with meta excluded, SHA-256'd; signatures over it verify","tags":["rfc","signatures","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.423927Z","id":"3245db3080aa2a9654497b9dfc710d52cabc1ee5592f06faee3e95aa120e0989","body":{"detail":"toolpath::v1::sign::path_author_input; tests/signatures.rs::moved_head_fails_both_path_signatures, ::reordered_steps_fail_the_author_signature; tests/jcs.rs::what_gets_signed.","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":745},"end":{"line":759},"content_hash":"33b2b5b39047676fc32c8522b7173e52f10f1e997781591549b5028c845b590e"},"summary":"Path author input is JCS({path, step_ids in steps order}); a moved head or reordered steps fail","tags":["rfc","signatures","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.423993Z","id":"1c7729f57b13e1d8723e8fa00ff3fb4eeeb321fb10d81873014f2f823ef7a681","body":{"detail":"Only the steps' own author signatures catch content changes (tests/signatures.rs::tampered_step_signature_is_caught_with_verify_steps: path author passes, verify_steps fails). Say so in the RFC, or sign step digests into the path input.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":759},"end":{"line":759},"content_hash":"b2e85074c6973f340a2b3a424f64d333537b6ad5525fed6148268325370c81ca"},"suggested_fix":"Either state that path author signatures attest order and ids only and step contents rely on step author signatures, or define step_ids as [{id, digest(step_author_input)}].","summary":"'I authored this path containing these steps' covers step ids only, not step contents: a changed diff still verifies the path author signature","tags":["rfc","signatures","security","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.424116Z","id":"84980c500c0a8d83100a57ba8269a29cb543a0355524035f65f93ffd0d74a1a2","body":{"detail":"toolpath::v1::sign::path_reviewer_input; tests/signatures.rs::signed_step_and_path_verify, ::moved_head_fails_both_path_signatures, ::reviewer_needs_its_timestamp.","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":761},"end":{"line":776},"content_hash":"c28d001bbe8d19d37de74e8d8d6a1a336d7a4b9dc53fdd9d75953c22631107da"},"summary":"Reviewer input is JCS({head, path_id, reviewed_at}); a moved head fails; reviewed_at is the signature timestamp, required","tags":["rfc","signatures","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.424161Z","id":"db4e36a0b6898d6532f215c51f4e757a227e209df95e53c6eba67d6b2eb3e666","body":{"detail":"crates/toolpath/tests/jcs.rs::rfc_canonicalization_example.","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":804},"end":{"line":804},"content_hash":"b4a465d915d9203eac014c80ce35ca77ed17df3b53a88eee7890149a2f6823a3"},"summary":"The canonicalization example is exact: the printed step canonicalizes to this string byte for byte","tags":["rfc","signatures","jcs","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.424198Z","id":"99fc1ce6a6617ef9a6bfbc4a4bd907b5889a145b23140f631209c64372091f65","body":{"detail":"toolpath::v1::sign::verify_step_signature (ssh keys); tests/signatures.rs::signed_step_and_path_verify, ::tampered_change_fails, ::wrong_key_and_resolver_lies_fail.","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":815},"end":{"line":818},"content_hash":"45d248975fdc72f9990e028c6a98158ce0c7d8baf55ea917522db584933e90d7"},"summary":"verify_step_signature implemented as written: canonical form, SHA-256, verify","tags":["rfc","signatures","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.424389Z","id":"a0f5fa7af6bf8c0f7d714c448ead548c68c30f098b27cf454f2c46c9557d1b8c","body":{"detail":"toolpath::v1::sign::verify_path_signatures; tests/signatures.rs::missing_required_scope_fails, ::signer_not_in_actors_fails, ::wrong_scope_canonical_form_fails, ::tampered_step_signature_is_caught_with_verify_steps.","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":820},"end":{"line":828},"content_hash":"eb3f993fbec8e03b75e38477b39fce7b08da62e01f3fad1e94ce9535d827ffee"},"summary":"verify_path_signatures implemented: each required scope must verify with the signer's key from meta.actors; optional step author checks; fails on any missing","tags":["rfc","signatures","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.424437Z","id":"41a0169146705346e3fc9205aab1dbf1348306133461427db388e94406157ebe","body":{"detail":"The implementation takes a caller resolver (Key → public key) and checks the resolved key's SHA256 fingerprint equals Key.fingerprint (tests/signatures.rs::wrong_key_and_resolver_lies_fail). The RFC should say where key material comes from (href, a keyring) and that fingerprints are checked.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":823},"end":{"line":823},"content_hash":"e7e43ace9ef8553b70214b90495767c214bdd25fafff9f19afa272463bbc2295"},"summary":"meta.actors[signer].keys holds no public key, only a type and fingerprint (plus href), so the key cannot be 'looked up' from the document","tags":["rfc","signatures","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.424478Z","id":"c50179d0938f269a2db17205cf3fa72980e4d400af2a08305cd5153febc484d3","body":{"detail":"verify_path_signatures refuses them as UnsupportedScope (tests/signatures.rs::scopes_without_a_canonical_form_are_refused). The RFC lists the scopes but defines what gets signed for two.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":395},"end":{"line":395},"content_hash":"5eadf0be002baa86da128ac4f01b51bac0c01320f14fd46fd8797dfd0272ddbc"},"summary":"Only author and reviewer have a canonical form; witness, ci and release signatures cannot be verified","tags":["rfc","signatures","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.424528Z","id":"c64c385f6ca18f8d53f374786ca77fd478e4b8a21848f7fe7785a64b0ed3037c","body":{"detail":"verify_path_signatures returns UnsupportedKeyType(\"gpg\") (tests/signatures.rs::gpg_and_sigstore_are_not_verified). The committed signed example (examples/path-03-signed-pr) carries placeholder gpg signatures that no code checks.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":834},"end":{"line":834},"content_hash":"2763fd9a9ddc7926d2e6709a5bd4a124334fc876ab376296ce7c315f5a9b9181"},"summary":"gpg signatures are not verified by any toolpath code","tags":["rfc","signatures","not-implemented","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.424613Z","id":"9ce9fc8981bae40a9f79e64edd157cfc9c25f14cc754ab6adacb19699c55092d","body":{"detail":"tests/signatures.rs (14 tests). Only Ed25519 is enabled. The RFC names no SSHSIG namespace; this implementation fixes it as 'toolpath' (toolpath::v1::sign::SSHSIG_NAMESPACE) — the RFC should state it, or signers and verifiers will disagree.","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":835},"end":{"line":835},"content_hash":"f9670fa5ccf88e5bda3897ef476543a6a2f934050b45d26a682f0766303597a2"},"summary":"ssh (Ed25519) signatures verify, in the SSHSIG format","tags":["rfc","signatures","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:26:43.424656Z","id":"e3cd7ca844071a7ef85e52ec2cc4c1666b156fb9d43f04c936c374480a855370","body":{"detail":"verify_path_signatures returns UnsupportedKeyType(\"sigstore\") (tests/signatures.rs::gpg_and_sigstore_are_not_verified).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":836},"end":{"line":836},"content_hash":"1df74d2cde505f1eaf39fe8b372cf969856d2ae2748803851b2efdeb05316d9b"},"summary":"sigstore bundles are not verified by any toolpath code","tags":["rfc","signatures","not-implemented","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.009157Z","id":"0c0f10918f96a2f7f0baeda814c72c03c74b51860f07541edbc6e978cd5a2c22","body":{"detail":"Schema root requires graph+paths; validate tests reject a missing field.","kind":"pass","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":106},"end":{"line":106},"content_hash":"24c2fb51fa823b52445145cfbbaa36b140cef6a118df0873370cdd12c3870070"},"summary":"RFC: Step and Path are not valid document roots — backed","tags":["claim:rfc-root-is-graph","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.009200Z","id":"31601b9be4eb3851c27060f218a63de22253b666d9bf6d36ac0fb18cbb9b965c","body":{"detail":"PathOrRef accepts any $ref string; nothing checks the target's extension or form.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":122},"end":{"line":122},"content_hash":"ebd9ce2deed09df50a67c84bcb86c6b8394d21294f3f99f4c96da9a3c91c4167"},"summary":"RFC: $ref MUST point to sealed .path.json — not enforced","tags":["claim:rfc-ref-must-be-sealed","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.009236Z","id":"efc22df166f41c2c150f652572a84105fc6265e4a19e4ad463aa889b949ee95f","body":{"detail":"Neither the schema nor path p validate checks ID uniqueness (no test for duplicates).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":131},"end":{"line":131},"content_hash":"2dea50f6a6a71516d20d4fd86a9edd1ed99b46246a28375180d62043e1bef824"},"summary":"RFC: step and path IDs unique in scope — not enforced","tags":["claim:rfc-id-uniqueness","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.009299Z","id":"d0ede3b31c61d47a2e7cc05c30f204c388255b2c352ecb60e637401921f215b5","body":{"detail":"Schema actor pattern; examples validated.","kind":"pass","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":270},"end":{"line":270},"content_hash":"566f2370c5e4318f5e9ef7640ba882b11a235e6ca997a696152e5a29824c8b0e"},"summary":"RFC: actor prefix human/agent/tool/ci — backed","tags":["claim:rfc-actor-prefix","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.009359Z","id":"2aa6cd7f6af0ae52d67eb2f99d96e67eda6ffeec78b2aac93d2c1937ec98661f","body":{"detail":"crates/toolpath/src/query.rs dead_ends + test_dead_ends.","kind":"pass","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":887},"end":{"line":887},"content_hash":"00cbee558b0238d88c194944e9231f24de59f497dc87f56c4ced1760affef0cb"},"summary":"RFC: dead_ends returns steps with no descendants leading to head — backed","tags":["claim:rfc-dead-ends-query","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.009402Z","id":"64f644fa36c165ab3db5b7101a93b141350ee377e4ee41f2eb5a0de5e56802dc","body":{"detail":"No crate canonicalizes for signing or verifies a signature; verify_step_signature / verify_path_signatures exist only as pseudocode.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":712},"end":{"line":712},"content_hash":"dfd7d6d839139a01c93c727b2af1f8fd7f8a3c7d57ee39adf6db4782c331969a"},"summary":"RFC: signatures over JCS canonical form — specified, unimplemented","tags":["claim:rfc-jcs-signatures","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.009444Z","id":"f215d88f4c54f6be361d475bac96efb2b4e41111b2d3483f84bdef3dcd6a1ca6","body":{"detail":"schema/toolpath.schema.json: actor pattern, date-time, signature scope enum, key type enum; schema_examples.","kind":"pass","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":966},"end":{"line":966},"content_hash":"279e444031eab3656ed52626a36ab20be63af5a48800f471486ce765ebe5d541"},"summary":"RFC: the schema enforces structure, actor format, timestamps, scopes, key types — backed","tags":["claim:rfc-schema-enforces","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.009482Z","id":"e294e1da11bdf085fd8f7be6dbb2f45bacf3d8f9ff9d4a591886fe6b5a0dd975","body":{"detail":"v1.0.0 and v1.1.0 both ship; legacy_kind_warns_once_per_path_and_still_validates.","kind":"pass","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":300},"end":{"line":300},"content_hash":"23bfed37131b6213a3237c7d256a1581fa378660f895364d197c0d35bc081d1f"},"summary":"RFC: kind URIs are immutable and semver-versioned — backed","tags":["claim:rfc-kinds-immutable","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.009580Z","id":"8d0491e6a44053ac43843c791386b77b5f8af79c0f24e2962eacca08c97ed918","body":{"detail":"toolpath-git and toolpath-github derive from git; no other VCS has a reader or a test.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":923},"end":{"line":923},"content_hash":"71a0201bbf95a98a0273848f1776fe518a87ee97657e7f1d89e887e5593e0138"},"summary":"RFC: VCS-agnostic, complements git, jj, Mercurial, Darcs, Fossil — only git implemented","tags":["claim:rfc-vcs-agnostic","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:21:41.398341Z","id":"dbcf534bf2a9b247c33ca8fffc593f4c9bd8f411f4ca04c1f82e1934242fb037","body":{"detail":"Session derivation emits a step per conversational turn between commits (document@claude-session.snap: 27 steps from one session); path p track builds steps between commits (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_track.rs, 61 tests, incl. a tool:formatter step).","kind":"pass","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":936},"end":{"line":936},"content_hash":"ae7981606c91d413ea6c5e3db40a6d785344da59b06748361b8352c37e73c0e2"},"summary":"RFC beyond-VCS 1, finer granularity — backed","tags":["claim:rfc-beyond-vcs-granularity","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:21:41.398425Z","id":"d53122caad978619f75b34bdf1797f32f04e942ca7db0c51a1057b31d014aa75","body":{"detail":"The format keeps dead ends structurally (crates/toolpath/src/query.rs dead_ends, test_dead_ends; examples/path-04-exploration). But only what was captured survives: git import cannot recover a deleted branch, and no session reader emits dead ends — toolpath-convo/toolpath-claude derive a linear chain (no fork/rewind handling; Claude sidechains are read with is_sidechain false). Only hand-built documents (p track, examples) carry dead ends.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":937},"end":{"line":938},"content_hash":"25c7d39f1e89f9cf471c9a286764bd072deb3bc864f3c8289e94378f7b438d15"},"summary":"RFC beyond-VCS 2, abandoned paths preserved — format yes, no producer emits dead ends","tags":["claim:rfc-beyond-vcs-abandoned-paths","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:21:41.398521Z","id":"8cbc14a3a5615d372a3a39a7bf555b4acc591e4201ba32dc8360331883149cdc","body":{"detail":"raw diffs exist (toolpath-convo file_write_diff; git/github derive) and structural conversation.append for agent sessions, but no producer emits a structural AST operation (rust.add_items is illustrative), and agent-session documents carry no meta.intent.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":939},"end":{"line":939},"content_hash":"cf8890c4537b8f394ce961ff76bd322c57aa82879226d3f761ad89220899e0d1"},"summary":"RFC beyond-VCS 3, raw diff + structural AST ops + intent — no producer emits AST ops","tags":["claim:rfc-beyond-vcs-multi-perspective","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:21:41.398575Z","id":"c773d1863587f6d589c8f0f5fd1a3e07a59e1373417fa68f54e59f29d07748d8","body":{"detail":"The schema has meta.actors identities; toolpath-git turns an author email into an actor slug (slugify_author) and toolpath-github names human:<login>, but neither fills identities; toolpath-convo writes identities: vec![] (derive.rs:546).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":940},"end":{"line":940},"content_hash":"52ac07cb199a43d2c10c241a4ca40cfcadf0cc7b373f08184094eb70374c7667"},"summary":"RFC beyond-VCS 4, actors linked to external identities — format only, producers leave identities empty","tags":["claim:rfc-beyond-vcs-actor-provenance","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:21:41.398619Z","id":"959be1227fcd26b03d93cd271507dceecfd02b15813b25c54f45414ab56a48f8","body":{"detail":"The schema holds scoped signatures and jsonl round-trips them (roundtrip_signed_with_actors, roundtrip_step_signature); no crate creates or verifies a signature yet (verification work is in progress elsewhere). Upgrade to pass once a verify test lands.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":941},"end":{"line":941},"content_hash":"6599929dc630a0f354e17dfd1e086e97639199135bb95cb90bb21cc1c8090666"},"summary":"RFC beyond-VCS 5, multi-party signatures — format only, nothing signs or verifies","tags":["claim:rfc-beyond-vcs-signatures","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:21:41.398661Z","id":"58188d3f23c2a4b0296e1aa89de7b6deb27b28adc4c51452990ab2624cc3e934","body":{"detail":"tool: actors exist in the schema and agents are captured from their logs, but nothing captures formatter or linter changes automatically; only path p track records them (cmd_track test with tool:formatter).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":942},"end":{"line":943},"content_hash":"edd4e53911ac479eeb36d37b0bc53eabdb1f986b423a0c6ba6f6bec7bb6385d1"},"summary":"RFC beyond-VCS 6, capture formatters and linters — only by hand","tags":["claim:rfc-beyond-vcs-tool-agnostic","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"RFC.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:25:18.513139Z","id":"ef0a2a8bcdc5e4b320c5622e9a8da28d01608a1ba132bd4f7d05045cac0d6a2f","body":{"detail":"origin/main 77dc16a RFC.md lines 303-304 (what toolpath.net/rfc shows today) read: 'The only one defined so far is https://toolpath.net/kinds/agent-coding-session/v1.0.0'. site/kinds/index.md lists v1.1.0 as current, and every document@<set>.snap carries meta.kind …/v1.1.0. The text on wip/bdelanghe at these lines (claims audit, toolpath #369) already says v1.1.0 and resolves it; resolve this record when #369 reaches main.","kind":"blocker","ref":"git:77dc16a","span":{"start":{"line":303},"end":{"line":307},"content_hash":"854f5dbe628d6f2931a467f9f94973cb18fbb1c0e5b4205c1db661fce9bb38fd"},"summary":"main's RFC.md:303 names agent-coding-session v1.0.0 as the only kind; the kinds page and every producer use v1.1.0","tags":["claim-main:rfc-only-kind-v1-0-0","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"FAQ.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:31:49.700392Z","id":"095e6d39a88bbe7d0a2b08d14003ebb9fac10b0b00680e16c232458fd35a510f","body":{"detail":"schema change keys; examples use bare paths and URLs; RFC Artifacts section.","kind":"pass","ref":"git:04afa53","span":{"start":{"line":113},"end":{"line":113},"content_hash":"8508e185cb863eb854ba0b429018f86a6c172d4a9c0674bee4cd48501357de64"},"summary":"FAQ.md: artifacts are identified by URL, bare paths relative to base — backed by schema and examples","tags":["claim:faqmd-artifact-urls","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"FAQ.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:31:49.700493Z","id":"d056fed48d981572c34c7283c08bd0cba12a371baf5826582da91400007a95ad","body":{"detail":"Path.steps is a flat array with parents (schema, types.rs); query.rs computes ancestors/dead ends by scanning.","kind":"pass","ref":"git:04afa53","span":{"start":{"line":189},"end":{"line":189},"content_hash":"eac069ed5dfe807422935e9dfca4d617266b059342ec05a87f7adbae2d91e300"},"summary":"FAQ.md open question 'storage': flat list with parent refs is the current approach — backed","tags":["claim:faqmd-flat-list","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"FAQ.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:31:49.700584Z","id":"b41e31c54a646e901b73b216ccdbbb22492687e45aa19b2ebd231d2326bd77dd","body":{"detail":"Granularity pass; abandoned paths, multi-perspective, actor identities, signatures, tool-agnostic capture are format-only or manual (see the RFC records).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:04afa53","span":{"start":{"line":138},"end":{"line":138},"content_hash":"80e4002f621ef00f7712f598cfd17ae26de37c990f9fa7946fc2d43e6c345345"},"summary":"FAQ.md beyond-VCS list — same six claims as RFC.md; see the rfc-beyond-vcs-* records (1 pass, 5 concerns)","tags":["claim:faqmd-beyond-vcs","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"README.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:51:19.885730Z","id":"5d43acf66231594cda8eae08ed71db4f272a39396e3081be16b14eedba2891c5","body":{"detail":"What and cost: document@ snapshots and the accounting contract (all 9 sets after pr/27). Why: agent sessions carry no meta.intent. Tried-and-abandoned: no session reader emits dead ends.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:04afa53","span":{"start":{"line":5},"end":{"line":7},"content_hash":"99ae9bad8190fd41a302bd8140b2d389e14c46ce9c1401061876dd5541c6db55"},"summary":"README: one schema records what, why, what was tried, what it cost — why and what-was-tried missing for agent sessions","tags":["claim:readme-open-format","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"README.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:51:19.885838Z","id":"796710e6f129ae02d29bd6406b1b393a28b2df5538c48e8ff328b306a5873162","body":{"detail":"ir@/projection@/round_trip@ for every pair; see claim parse-in-project-out.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:04afa53","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":13},"content_hash":"67a501e60e713f388b58a4a9e0ace8c116b4106692fc0a6ac4882c3718f7442b"},"summary":"README: reads all seven and writes them back — backed for read and write, with undeclared losses and invented values on write","tags":["claim:readme-reads-all-writes-back","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
